### Example: Gate CI on structural violations
  {{ ref: 37db2572-f788-81a4-b87b-cd0325724fdc }}
  **When to use:** Continuous enforcement — fail the build when someone introduces a cycle or a production → test import.
  --{ ref: 37db2572-f788-81a4-b87b-cd0325724fdc }--
  {{ ref: 37db2572-f788-81a4-9477-c2f7fafba51f }}
  **Entry point:** `strata violations`
  --{ ref: 37db2572-f788-81a4-9477-c2f7fafba51f }--
  {{ ref: 37db2572-f788-810b-adca-d47688ef90dd }}
  **Outcome:** A violation table; exit code `2` if any `--fail-on` class is present.
  --{ ref: 37db2572-f788-810b-adca-d47688ef90dd }--
  {{ ref: 37db2572-f788-81a5-823b-d18c6131fa5e }}
  **Command & expected output:**
  --{ ref: 37db2572-f788-81a5-823b-d18c6131fa5e }--
  {{ ref: 30edf5b2-0d99-47df-a00d-03e34c5f8394 }}
  ```bash
  $ strata violations --root . --fail-on cycle,polarity
  KIND      SEVERITY    LOCATION                                  DETAIL
  cycle     violation   packages/data/{store.rs, codec.rs}        2-file cycle; break codec.rs -> store.rs (w=1.0, exact)
  polarity  violation   packages/api/server.ts -> tests/util.ts   production imports test support
  capacity  borderline  packages/core/engine.rs                   263 prod sloc (cap 250, +5%)
  $ echo $?
  2
  ```
  --{ ref: 30edf5b2-0d99-47df-a00d-03e34c5f8394 }--
  {{ ref: 37db2572-f788-815e-a723-c2f553b47cb0 }}
  **Errors to expect:** `ConfigInvalid` → unknown class name in `--fail-on`.
  --{ ref: 37db2572-f788-815e-a723-c2f553b47cb0 }--
  {{ ref: 37db2572-f788-8131-9de6-d704c41d2848 }}
  **Notes:** `borderline` findings (within ±10% of a cap) never trigger exit `2` — they absorb formatter churn.
  --{ ref: 37db2572-f788-8131-9de6-d704c41d2848 }--
--{ ref: 37db2572-f788-818a-9852-fa7c2d95dc32 }--

